    "result_text": "All 6 tests pass, build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the derived `riskFlag` on the owner response so it is `true` when **any** of the three signals hold \u2014 possible duplicate, disposable-adjacent email domain, or city over its soft capacity \u2014 and `false` otherwise.\n\nThe two count-based signals (possible duplicate, over-soft-capacity) are already captured at creation time on the entity (`possibleDuplicate`, `capacityWarning`), so `riskFlag` reuses those point-in-time snapshots rather than recomputing them. Only the third signal \u2014 **disposable-adjacent** \u2014 was new.\n\nChanges, each kept to a single responsibility:\n\n- **`OwnerEmails`** \u2014 added `isDisposableAdjacentDomain(email)` alongside the existing `isDisposableDomain`. \"Disposable-adjacent\" means the domain shares a disposable provider's *registrable label* (the `mailinator` of `mailinator.com`), so subdomains (`inbox.mailinator.com`) and alternate TLDs (`mailinator.net`) count, while unrelated lookalikes (`mymailinator.com`) don't. I refactored the shared `@`/domain parsing into private `domainOf` / `registrableLabel` helpers so both blocklist and adjacency checks use one code path.\n\n- **`OwnerRisk`** (new, public) \u2014 the aggregator: `flag(owner)` OR-combines the three conditions, delegating email adjacency to `OwnerEmails` and reading the two stored flags via `Boolean.TRUE.equals(...)` (null-safe for owners predating the flags).\n\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 a `riskFlag(owner)` default method delegating to `OwnerRisk.flag`, wired with a `@Mapping` expression exactly like the other derived read-only fields.\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `riskFlag` read-only boolean to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field on build.\n\nThe existing acceptance test (`riskFlag` false for a normal owner) and all others stay green.",
